  "question": {
    "text": "Let P be the set of seven digit numbers with sum of their digits equal to 11 . If the numbers in P are formed by using the digits 1,2 and 3 only, then the number of elements in the set \\(P\\) is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "n1krw",
      "text": "173",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oLVQu",
      "text": "164",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BgjZG",
      "text": "158",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eXGmA",
      "text": "161",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) number of numbers created using\n$1111133=\\frac{7!}{5!2!} \\Rightarrow 21$\n(ii) number of numbers created using\n$1111223=\\frac{7!}{4!2!} \\Rightarrow 105$\n(iii) number of numbers created using\n$1112222=\\frac{7!}{4!3!} \\Rightarrow 35$\n\nTotal $=161$",
    "image": null
  },
